        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Saga's Chicago study 1 reported a year-two bound of 0.305 study-sample standard deviations for CPS math test (study sample Z), assuming only first-year benefits persist.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "property": {
          "$bytes": "9b1f76ff9711404c861e59dc3fa7d037"
        },
        "value": {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Table 6, p. 753 reports 0.305 (SE 0.067; N=1640; FDR q=0.001). This bound assumes nonnegative benefits and zero incremental second-year benefit; it is not a point effect or confidence limit.",
          "language": {
            "$bytes": "090adac0fca4822e8e719263e67620ec"
          }
        }
